<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The launch colours, and why they are duplicated here.

    Every other colour in this app lives in `JarvisPalette` and is chosen at
    runtime, because the user picks a theme. The splash cannot wait for that: the
    window is painted by the system before a single line of Kotlin runs, so its
    colour has to be a static resource compiled into the APK.

    This is Arc's background — the default theme, and what a first launch shows.
    Someone running the Forge theme gets a brief Arc-coloured splash, which is the
    correct trade: the alternative is the window having no colour at all until the
    process starts, which is the white flash this replaces.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="launch_background">#FF04101E</color>
</resources>
